# Build output
bin/
obj/

# IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user

# Runtime-generated logs
src/RoutinePlanner.Web/logs/*.log

# The SQLite databases are LIVE DATA and are deliberately not tracked.
#
# campus.sqlite3 used to be committed, and it held real, named academics with their subject
# allocations and their weekly working hours. That is personal data, this repository has a public
# remote, and a binary database is not reviewable in a diff either. A fresh clone now starts with no
# database at all — the app creates an empty one on first use — and
# `dotnet run --project src/RoutinePlanner.Web -- --seed` fills it with the invented teachers in
# App_Data/seed/teachers.seed.json.
#
# Untracking them also means `dotnet run` can no longer dirty the working tree by doing nothing more
# than what the app is for. It used to write straight into the tracked file, so adding a teacher
# showed up as a binary diff and `git checkout` silently discarded it.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
